#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:398
msgid "Checkout"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:399
msgid ""
"How the checkout delivery picker behaves. Reorder couriers by dragging their "
"tabs above; prices show in the store currency."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:400
msgid "Default courier"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:401
msgid ""
"Which courier is pre-selected at checkout (its first delivery option is the "
"default)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:403
msgid "Where the delivery block goes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:404
msgid ""
"The couriers, their prices and the fields of the one chosen move together as "
"one block. “With the order review” leaves them where WooCommerce puts "
"shipping rates, at the bottom of the page. “Under the customer details” "
"moves the whole block up to just after the phone number: on a checkout with "
"add-ons, gift options or a long totals table the couriers are otherwise the "
"very last thing a customer reaches, after everything optional. This is for "
"the classic (shortcode) checkout; the block checkout renders in React and "
"keeps the rates where they are."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:405
msgid "With the order review (default)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:406
msgid "Under the customer details, after the phone"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:408
msgid "Checkout dropdown results"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:409
msgid ""
"How many matches the city and street searches return. Office lists are never "
"limited - the whole list for the chosen city is loaded. Raise it if "
"customers report not finding their town; very high values make each "
"keystroke slower on phones."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:411
msgid "Preload city lists"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:412
msgid ""
"Embed each courier’s office/APS city list so those dropdowns open instantly. "
"Address search stays live. Recommended."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:413
msgid "Interactive map of all couriers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:414
msgid ""
"Adds one map above the shipping methods showing every enabled courier’s "
"offices and lockers for a city at once, with each courier’s price, so a "
"customer can choose by where they will collect rather than by courier. "
"Choosing a point fills in the courier, delivery type and office. Each "
"courier keeps its own map button as well. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:416
msgid "“Nearest to you” on the map"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:417
msgid ""
"On the interactive map, a pin the customer can move (it starts on the office "
"already chosen, or the town centre, and “find me” puts it on their location) "
"and how far each pickup point is from it. The distances are worked out in "
"the customer’s own browser; their position is never stored on the site and "
"is forgotten when they leave the page. The one time the coordinates leave "
"the browser is when the customer presses “find me” before naming a town - "
"those are then reverse-geocoded to fill the town in for them (see the "
"External services notice). On by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:419
msgid "Map hint: closest"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:420
msgid ""
"Above the list of points, the one closest to the pin on the map, with its "
"distance, price and courier. Needs “Nearest to you”. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:422
msgid "Map hint: cheapest"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:423
msgid ""
"Above the list of points, the cheapest one (the nearest of them when several "
"cost the same), with its price and courier. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:425
msgid "Map hint: to the address"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:426
msgid ""
"Above the list of points, the lowest price of delivery to the address and "
"its courier; pressing it chooses that delivery at the checkout. On by "
"default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:428
msgid "Address map picker"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:429
msgid ""
"Adds a “Choose on map” pin picker to address delivery that fills the address "
"automatically. When a customer drops a pin, its coordinates are sent to "
"OpenStreetMap Nominatim (or Google, if a key is set below) to look up the "
"address. Off by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:430
msgid "Google Maps API key (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:431
msgid ""
"Used for one thing only: turning a point picked on the map into an address. "
"Leave it empty and OpenStreetMap Nominatim does that free of charge; the "
"maps themselves are OpenStreetMap either way. The key needs Google’s "
"“Geocoding API” and is only ever used from the server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:433
msgid "Use the plugin’s own address fields"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:434
msgid ""
"Remove WooCommerce’s Address / City / Region / Post code at checkout - the "
"courier’s city, office or automat chosen here IS the delivery address, and "
"asking twice lets the two disagree. Turn this off if your store also ships "
"some other way and needs those fields. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:436
msgid "Hide the cart shipping calculator"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:437
msgid ""
"Hide WooCommerce’s “Calculate shipping” box on the cart. It prices a "
"delivery to a post code, while every price here is for the office, automat "
"or address picked at checkout - so it would show a number the customer never "
"pays. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:439
msgid "Require an e-mail address"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:440
msgid ""
"Insist on an e-mail address at checkout. The plugin makes the field optional "
"by default - a courier waybill is built with the phone number, not with an e-"
"mail - so turn this on if your shop needs the address for its own order e-"
"mails or invoices. The phone number is always required. Do not also hide the "
"e-mail field below: a required field nobody can see cannot be filled in, and "
"the order cannot be placed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:442
msgid "Hide \"Country\" field"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:443
msgid "Hidden checkout fields (CSS selectors)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:444
msgid ""
"Comma-separated CSS selectors to hide on checkout (e.g. "
"#billing_company_field, .cart-subtotal)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:449
msgid "Prices & display"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:450
msgid "Shipping estimate on the cart"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:451
msgid ""
"On the cart page, show a rough cached shipping price per courier/option (the "
"exact price is calculated at checkout). Off by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:452
msgid "Free shipping label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:453
msgid ""
"Text shown for the shipping price when a method is free (e.g. “Free "
"shipping”)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:457
msgid "Orders list"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:458
msgid ""
"Colour each order row by its courier, so the mix of couriers in the list is "
"readable at a glance. Pick a normal, saturated colour - the row is painted "
"with a pale version of it, keeping the text readable. Clear a colour to "
"leave that courier untinted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:459
msgid "Colour orders by courier"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:460
msgid "Tint each row in the orders list with its courier’s colour."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:464
#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:723
msgid "Cash on delivery (наложен платеж)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:465
msgid ""
"How you fiscalise collected COD. With ППП (no cash register), a courier that "
"lacks ППП needs prepayment at checkout (or is hidden). Enable ППП per "
"courier on its tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:466
msgid "COD fiscalisation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:468
msgid "I issue the receipt myself (I have a cash register)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:469
msgid "I rely on the courier's postal money transfer / ППП (no cash register)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:474
msgid "Label generation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:477
msgid ""
"Automatically generate a shipping label when an order reaches the status "
"below. This is the default for every courier; each courier's own tab can "
"overrule it - which matters because issuing a waybill is what tells some "
"couriers a parcel is ready to be collected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:478
msgid "Trigger status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:481
msgid "Wait for the dispatch day"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:482
msgid ""
"When the order names the day it ships (a delivery-date plugin such as Order "
"Delivery Date stamps it on the order), issue the automatic waybill on the "
"morning of that day instead of the moment the order reaches the status "
"above. A waybill is a live shipment at the courier from the moment it "
"exists: some couriers come for it the same day, and one issued weeks early "
"sits at the courier for weeks. An order that names no day is labelled at "
"once, and generating by hand is never held back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:485
msgid "Share customer email with courier"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:486
msgid ""
"Put the customer’s e-mail on the shipment for courier notifications, when "
"provided."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:488
msgid "Re-issue the waybill when the order changes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:489
msgid ""
"If an order that already has a waybill is edited in a way the courier needs "
"to know about - the delivery address, the contents, the weight or the amount "
"to collect - void it and issue a new one automatically. Edits that do not "
"affect the shipment (status, notes) never trigger it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:491
msgid "Shipment contents (description)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:492
msgid ""
"Short description of the parcel contents, printed on every courier's waybill "
"(e.g. “Хранителни добавки”). Empty = a generic value."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:495
msgid "Measure the parcel from the order"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:496
msgid ""
"Work out each parcel's size from the products in the order instead of "
"declaring the same default for every shipment: the footprint of the largest "
"item, and the height that makes the parcel hold exactly what was ordered, "
"plus the packaging allowance below. This is what a locker compartment is "
"picked by, so an order that no longer fits a small box stops being booked "
"into one. A product with no dimensions of its own counts as the default "
"parcel below - fill your products in for this to be worth anything."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:499
msgid "Packaging allowance (x)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:500
msgid ""
"How much bigger the parcel is than the goods inside it - the bag, the air "
"between the items, the padding. 1.1 adds ten per cent to the measured "
"volume. 1 = the goods exactly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:503
msgid "Packaging weight (kg)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:504
msgid ""
"Added to the weight of the ordered products on every waybill - the bag or "
"box, the tape, the padding. Not added when the products carry no weight at "
"all, because the default weight below is already a whole parcel. 0 = do not "
"count it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:506
msgid "Default parcel length (cm)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:507
#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:510
#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:513
msgid ""
"Default parcel size sent to every courier whose API takes dimensions (a "
"locker parcel must fit its box), used when an order has none of its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:509
msgid "Default parcel width (cm)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:512
msgid "Default parcel height (cm)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:515
msgid "Default parcel weight (kg)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:516
msgid ""
"Weight declared on the waybill when none of the ordered products has a "
"weight set. Set weights on your products to have the real weight sent "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:520
msgid "Shipment tracking"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:521
msgid ""
"Poll couriers for tracking updates and note them on the order (BOX NOW uses "
"its webhook). Only active shipments from the last 45 days."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:522
msgid "Auto-update tracking"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:524
msgid "Off"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:525
#: includes/class-bgcouriers-plugin.php:100
